    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d298-a10">

                <pb facs="0788" n="666" sameAs="frus:frus1889/pg666"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 10 in No.
                    27—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Pierce to administrator of customs.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Matanzas</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-09-26"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 26,
                        1888</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>I have the honor to inclose for your consideration the copy of a communication
                    from Messrs. Bea, Bellido &amp; Co. of this city, referring to a fine imposed on
                    the American steam-ship <hi rendition="#italic">Manhattan</hi> for packages
                    undelivered to that custom-house, as also the certificate of the Spanish
                    consul-general at New York, to which the said communication refers.</p>
                <p>May God keep you many years.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Frank H. Pierce.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
